{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01, which is about implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n1. For each call, subtract `loss_with_call` from `loss_without_call` to get the gain\n2. Normalize gain by dividing by `prediction_tokens` (at least one token)\n3. Accept a call if it's parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics\n\nLet me trace through the logic:\n\nFor each call:\n- `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n- `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens` (prediction_tokens \u003e= 1)\n- `accepted = parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n\nThe output should be:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of call_ids where accepted=True\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `call_id`, `accepted`, `normalized_gain`\n\nLet me verify with case 0:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true, 0.31253119 \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true, \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true, \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079 - wait let me recalculate: 0.75953930/5 = 0.15190786, parseable=true, \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, normalized = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true, 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05 → rejected\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, normalized = 0.76393214/4 = 0.190983035, parseable=true, \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call5\"]\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Validate prediction_tokens \u003e= 1\n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 10)  # Need to figure out rounding\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThe artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify how many decimal places. I'll use a reasonable number like 10 significant digits or just return the float as-is. Actually, I'll round to a reasonable precision - let me check the schema: normalized_gain is just \"type\": \"number\" so any float should be fine.\n\nLet me also consider validation - the artifact says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\"\n\nI should validate:\n- threshold is present\n- calls is present and is a list\n- Each call has required fields\n- prediction_tokens \u003e= 1\n\nLet me write the complete implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    \n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: calls\")\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\n        for field in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field '{field}' in call at index {i}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me verify case 002 which has a call with `parseable: false`:\n- call4: parseable=false → rejected regardless of normalized_gain\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON string inside the required envelope `{\"implementation\": \"...python code...\"}`.\n\nLet me encode it properly as a JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field '{field}' in call at index {i}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01S